              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Hallward-Drimieier, the judgment bar protects a government employee by precluding later suits."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Hallward-Drimieier",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "e5a5bec18281bef46949e18773c41cf7ed858b60d69f3fac5849863adec2571c",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-e5a5bec18281-0001-0003"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 21,
                "start": 21
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Hallward-Drimieier, statute 1346(b) bars any action related to the same subject matter after a judgment that finally resolves the United States\u2019 liability."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Hallward-Driemeier",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "e5a5bec18281bef46949e18773c41cf7ed858b60d69f3fac5849863adec2571c",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-e5a5bec18281-0002-0004"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 48,
                "start": 47
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Hallward-Driemeier, the Westfall Act confers official immunity, meaning any action related to the same subject matter is precluded."
        }
      ],
